"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia commit, DL Marcellus Young Casario died after 'sudden medical emergency'","description":"Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia football commit, died Friday after experiencing a \"sudden medical emergency,\" according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD 'infuriated' with SEC, Ole Miss for Sunday game","description":"AD Roger Denny took aim at the SEC and Ole Miss about Oklahoma's game being moved to Sunday, calling it an \"inexplicable\" situation that \"unfairly burdens\" the Sooners.","published":"2026-11-14T21:47:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Tait Reynolds suffers leg injury on slide","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds was knocked out of the Tigers' game against Georgia Tech on Saturday after injuring his knee on a run play.","published":"2026-11-14T21:42:04.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T20:09:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State's Jeremiah Smith sets Big Ten receiving record","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards during the first half vs. Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T21:26:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tracking Ohio State WR Jeremiah Smith's record-setting 2026 season","description":"Ohio State's superstar receiver has made breaking records a weekly occurrence this fall.","published":"2026-11-14T18:05:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50142903/jeremiah-smith-ohio-state-record-tracker","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Injured Russell starts, throws 3 TDs as Alabama survives Vandy","description":"No. 3 Alabama made a last-second decision to start Keelon Russell in a 21-6 win over Vanderbilt after the quarterback looked better than anticipated in pregame warmups.","published":"2026-11-14T21:59:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480988/alabama-makes-last-second-call-start-qb-keelon-russell","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Maryland QB Malik Washington doesn't start vs. Wisconsin","description":"Maryland quarterback Malik Washington did not start against Wisconsin as he continues to deal with a lower-body injury.","published":"2026-11-14T17:50:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480722/source-maryland-qb-malik-washington-start-vs-wisconsin","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado upsets No. 14 Houston for first AP top-15 win since 2007","description":"Colorado posted its first victory over an AP top-15 team since 2007 in beating No. 14 Houston 42-32 and slightly cooled down the hot seat for coach Deion Sanders.","published":"2026-11-14T14:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50479172/colorado-upsets-no-14-houston-1st-ap-top-15-win-2007","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5136784/francis-brewu","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Francis Brewu","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:30Z","intro":"Francis Brewu (born January 17, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In January 2024, Brewu enrolled early at Pittsburgh. He quickly impressed during spring camp due to his size and technique and was moved off of the scout team. He was also named the strongest player on the team by his teammates. Prior to the 2024 season, Brewu was named number 77 on Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List. During the season he played in 12 games with one start and totaled 15 tackles, three tackles for loss and 1.5 sacks. He was also named to the Pro Football Focus (PFF) All-Freshman Team at the end of the season. In December 2024, Brewu announced he would return to the Panthers for 2025. On August 4, 2025, Brewu was again named to Feldman's Freaks List, this time at number 24. In 2025 Brewu started 12 games for the Panthers in which he led all Pitt interior defensive linemen in tackles. Due to his performance, Brewu gained recognition as an Honorable Mention All-ACC selection. On January 6, 2026, Brewu entered the transfer portal, and chose to transfer to the Notre Dame Fighting Irish on January 13. On August 10, 2026, Brewu was named to Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List for the third consecutive season."}]}}